            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your body is still adapting to exogenous T. Aromatization patterns, energy fluctuations, and trough effects are all still emerging. Give it 3–6 months of consistent dosing to establish a clear pattern."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your brain's neural architecture has been androgen-adapted for years. The androgen receptor and local-aromatization signaling that shaped this adaptation continues to maintain it as an ongoing, active state." : {
      "comment" : "Long-term insight into the user's brain's neural architecture after 36 months of testosterone exposure.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Your brain's neural architecture is fully adapted. Consistent hormone levels maintain ongoing neuroprotection, synaptic health, and emotional stability — a continuous, active state." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
